--   Pass 5 producer (round six, `scP_sp`)
-- statement:
--   **Pass 5 producer.** `L = fA q s` on `30`, `|L|` on `31`, `n' ≥ s` on `iN`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegILSrc10`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.Src.scP_sp (s0 : IState HS) (F : Fin HS → List ℤ) {iN : Fin HS} (fN : Free iN)
--       (s : ℕ) (q : ℕ → Bool) {n' A : ℕ} {L30 L31 LN : List ℤ}
--       (h30 : F 30 = zLs (fA q s) ++ L30) (h31 : F 31 = ((fA q s).length : ℤ) :: L31)
--       (hGN : F iN = (n' : ℤ) :: LN) (hsn : s ≤ n') (hnA : n' ≤ 2 ^ A) (hA : 2 ≤ A) :
--       Sp (scP iN) (encK s0 F)
--         (encK s0 (update F 44 (srcTab (sSrc (fA q s)) (fun _ => 0) n' ++ F 44)))
--         ((s + n' + 2) * (200 * uC A DD))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, source-table producers, part 10: pass 5 (`scSrc`, the scatter)
--
--   For `L = (range s).filter q` (`= LJ = Jlist (mkBlocks …)`) on `30` and `|L|` on `31`, `n'` (`≥ s`)
--   on `iN`: `scP iN` moves `L` reversed onto `15`, pushes the count `c = |L|` on `13`, and for
--   `u = n' - 1, …, 0` pushes `0` and `code (scSrc u)` on `44` (`scSrc u = some (idxOf u)` if `u ∈ L`):
--   `u ∈ L` iff `c > 0` and the top of `15` (the largest remaining entry, always `≤ u`) equals `u`,
--   in which case the code is `c - 1`, the entry moves back to `30` and `c` decreases. Output:
--   `44 := srcTab (sSrc L) (fun _ => 0) n' ++ F 44`, everything else unchanged. Theorem `scP_sp`.
